+        # LOCAL PATCH: make the allocator FAIL instead of silently spilling to
+        # host memory.
+        #
+        # THE BUG THIS FIXES. Three identical batch-100 calls, same code, same
+        # batch size, measured on this box (RTX 4090, 24 GB, WSL2):
+        #   audio_T=147456  dt=  0.891 s  peak_reserved=16.35 GB  num_ooms=0
+        #   audio_T=157952  dt=  2.330 s  peak_reserved=24.83 GB  num_ooms=0
+        #   audio_T=198144  dt=398.892 s  peak_reserved=33.10 GB  num_ooms=0
+        # 33.10 GB reserved on a 24 GB card with num_ooms=0. The NVIDIA WSL2
+        # driver's sysmem-fallback policy satisfies the cudaMalloc out of host
+        # memory rather than failing, so `except torch.cuda.OutOfMemoryError`
+        # below can never fire and the run silently thrashes across PCIe --
+        # a measured 448x on one batch. It is intermittent at a fixed batch
+        # size because VITS' duration predictor is stochastic
+        # (noise_scale_w=0.8), so y_lengths.max() -- which sizes the decoder
+        # tensor for the WHOLE batch -- varies per batch. That is exactly the
+        # "wedged at batch 100, fine at batch 25" symptom in docs/HANDOFF.md.
+        #
+        # WHAT THIS CHANGES. With a fraction set, an over-large batch raises
+        # OutOfMemoryError, auto_reduce_batch_size retries at a smaller batch,
+        # and the run continues in seconds instead of stalling for minutes.
+        # NOTE HONESTLY: a reduced batch DOES change generated audio, because
+        # audio_float_to_int16 normalises by np.max(np.abs(audio)) over the
+        # whole (batch, 1, T) array -- batch composition sets every clip's
+        # gain. That is the behaviour auto_reduce_batch_size already asks for
+        # by name; this patch only makes it reachable. Pass
+        # cuda_memory_fraction=None to restore the old (thrashing) behaviour.
+        if cuda_memory_fraction is not None:
+            torch.cuda.set_per_process_memory_fraction(float(cuda_memory_fraction))
+            _LOGGER.debug(
+                "Capped CUDA allocations at %.2f of device memory so that "
+                "oversized batches raise OutOfMemoryError instead of spilling "
+                "to host memory", cuda_memory_fraction,
+            )
+
